  "Version": "1.21.7",
  "Authors@R": "c(\nperson(\"Ellis\", \"Patrick\", , \"ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au\", role = c(\"aut\", \"cre\")),\nperson(\"Nicolas\", \"Canete\", , \"nicolas.canete@sydney.edu.au\", role = \"aut\"),\nperson(\"Nicholas\", \"Robertson\", , \"nicholas.robertson@sydney.edu.au\", role = \"ctb\"),\nperson(\"Alex\", \"Qin\", , \"alex.qin@sydney.edu.au\", role = \"ctb\"),\nperson(\"Shreya\", \"Rao\", email = \"shreya.rajeshrao@sydney.edu.au\", role = \"ctb\"),\nperson(\"Farhan\", \"Ameen\", email = \"fame2827@uni.sydney.edu.au\", role = \"ctb\")\n)",
  "Description": "lisaClust provides a series of functions to identify and\nvisualise regions of tissue where spatial associations between\ncell-types is similar. This package can be used to provide a\nhigh-level summary of cell-type colocalization in multiplexed\nimaging data that has been segmented at a single-cell\nresolution.",
