  "_commit": {
    "id": "262fe35db624990cca97d6f88c5bd7d3b8e3fe35",
    "author": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "committer": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "message": "1.21.7: concave windows from a C++ port of concaveman; concaveman no longer needed\n\nThe core's concaveman.cpp ports the JavaScript that the R package\nconcaveman 1.2.0 runs in V8 (concaveman, rbush, tinyqueue, the monotone\nhull and robust orientation, and V8's own exp and log), with the rounding\nits R interface applies to the input. On the windows of all 41 Keren\nimages (three window.length values), the diabetesData images and 260\nsynthetic cases (ties, duplicates, collinear points, tiny inputs) it gives\npolygons identical to concaveman::concaveman(), about 7 times faster. The\ntests compare it with polygons saved from concaveman.\n\nhatchingPlot(), whose default window is \"concave\", works without\nconcaveman again (1.21.6 had moved it to Suggests).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TfsjwkbDbHkX4kJZNe4ER4\n",
    "time": 1791598712
  },
